  "narrative": {
    "intro": "DLT Solutions reported $244M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. DLT Solutions received 298 awards so far, with an average award size of $818K, and obligations are down 13.7% year over year. DLT Solutions has a multi-year profile that shows FY21 obligations of $306M, FY22 obligations of $282M, FY23 obligations of $239M, FY24 obligations of $273M, and FY25 obligations of $282M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of DLT Solutions, with $204M in obligations this fiscal year to date. DLT Solutions also has non-DoD customers, including the Department of Justice with $12.3M and the Department of Homeland Security with $5.6M. DLT Solutions concentrates most revenue in Other Computer Related Services at $219M, followed by Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $17.8M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $6.2M. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 to date figures are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are DLT Solutions top customers this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $204M with DLT Solutions in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $12.3M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $5.6M. The Department of Labor, Department of Transportation, and General Services Administration also appear among the top buyers with $3.9M, $3.3M, and $3.2M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive DLT Solutions federal sales?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest market for DLT Solutions with $219M in obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services follow with $17.8M and $6.2M respectively. Smaller markets include Other General Government Support at $645K and Software Publishers at $190K and $135K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
