      "q": "How much does DLT Solutions make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "DLT Solutions has $244M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. DLT Solutions received 298 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $818K and obligations down 13.7% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from DLT Solutions?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of DLT Solutions with $204M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other federal buyers include the Department of Justice with $12.3M, the Department of Homeland Security with $5.6M, the Department of Labor with $3.9M, and the General Services Administration with $3.2M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does DLT Solutions sell to the government?",
      "a": "DLT Solutions sells mostly computer-related services and technology products to the government, led by Other Computer Related Services at $219M. DLT Solutions also has obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $17.8M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $6.2M, plus smaller obligations in Software Publishers and Other General Government Support."
